    "findings": [
      {
        "area": "native_controller",
        "verdict": "supported_static",
        "detail": "qualify_f020_dma limits selection to generic plus three exact F020 parts, exact 8KiB SRAM or generic None, native controller base/version and two physical channels, real IRQ9/10 and reserved11, native scalar fields/access, five descriptor layouts and own-source typed enum encodings. Actual sanitized metapac names/types match the assertions; shared RCC metadata is reused and checked."
      },
      {
        "area": "direction_qualification",
        "verdict": "supported_static",
        "detail": "UART TX/RX and SPI policies are separate. Existing x030/L083 retain exact two-route inventories, one unrestricted six-bit route per direction and distinct RX/TX selectors. RX is asserted a subset of TX. F020 receives only UART1/2/3 TX; request emission filters peripheral+signal pairs. x030 raw route inventory and L083 UART/SPI RX+TX remain preserved."
      },
      {
        "area": "runtime_delta",
        "verdict": "exact_remaining_source_identity",
        "detail": "After full comment/cfg line deletion, all remaining bytes of lib.rs, dma.rs and usart.rs equal accepted Stage83 backups. Both lib DMA gates broaden to the native cfg. Nine geometry guards suppress CH3-5 in three matches. No runtime algorithm, fence, signature or wake rewrite occurred. CFG semantics were separately reviewed rather than inferred from identity."
      },
      {
        "area": "cfg_partition",
        "verdict": "43_of_43_match",
        "detail": "36 USART and seven shared DMA guards match the approved independent design map. There is no standalone uart_dma spelling. RX-only state/methods and combined UART constructor do not compile on F020; start_read and pair admission require RX/SPI. Ordinary/native idle/buffered imports and owners retain independent guards."
      },
      {
        "area": "ownership_terminal",
        "verdict": "supported_static_no_hardware_claim",
        "detail": "Admission, raw revocation, full SRAM/range/alignment/overlap checks, TC/no-TE and STATUS5 corroboration, software-only SOFTSRC, first-poll recording, own-channel clear/masking, permanent error quarantine, pending/error Drop resource retention and no early-abort guarantee remain intact. Current native PAC exposes the correct 0xFFFFFFFF ICR helpers and four-field projection; no runtime ICR RMW."
      },
      {
        "area": "stage83_seam",
        "verdict": "preserved",
        "detail": "Actual ring preparation, RX-only detach, static DMA construction, retained clock/configuration, no-ring RX DMA FE/PE handling with RC masked, inactive-before-MMIO guard and separate L083 partner dispatch are unchanged. UART and DMA wakes remain after their outer CS. No buffered-DMA attachment or owner conversion appears."
      },
      {
        "area": "examples",
        "verdict": "supported_static",
        "detail": "Seven files match frozen author bytes. Three exact chip features and two explicit normal bins; memory.x derived from exact metadata. Copy app owns disjoint 512-byte array set, starts both transfers before awaiting, checks full results and reuses only successful owners. TX app owns two UART/channel/pin/static stages on approved routes, two Embassy task instances, ordinary flash/local messages larger than 32-byte stages, and awaits flush. No raw register or unsafe DMA entry, recovery, abort, buffer replacement or synthetic harness."
      },
      {
        "area": "example_dependencies",
        "verdict": "unchanged_89_dependency_records",
        "detail": "Dependency/build-dependency/profile declarations match uart-dma-tx. All 89 dependency lock records match; root package changes only its name. All eight planned F020 main/clean command tuples now resolve features and bin paths without execution."
      }
    ],
