  "ownership_and_lifecycle": [
    "Safe copy accepts owned disjoint full-range static SRAM buffers and conservatively admits only the clean startup state. Raw channel acquisition permanently revokes safe-copy admission.",
    "Copy release requires a recorded terminal success with no TE, STATUS 5 and SOFTSRC clear. Hardware TX completion uses terminal success and STATUS 5 without the software-only SOFTSRC condition.",
    "Error, cancellation and pending Drop do not establish bus drain. Unconfirmed resources remain permanently retained; late TC does not recover an error. Safe owned-copy Drop may wait indefinitely. No early-abort recovery or channel-reset release was added.",
    "Staged UART TX starts the channel before DMATX, closes the request before successful resource retirement, uses the existing memory fence, and flushes through UART TXBUSY. Pending/error Drop retains staging, channel, pin and UART configuration/clock ownership.",
    "Actual Stage83 ring initialization/detachment and lifecycle handling remain intact. No-ring DMA RX leaves RDR untouched, masks receive-complete delivery and preserves FE/PE handling. Shared L083 dispatch examines each instance independently and avoids inactive MMIO.",
    "UART and DMA wakers run after the outer critical section. No buffered RX plus DMA constructor or owner conversion was added."
  ],
